These examples instrument an OpenMP matrix multiply in C (c), C++ (c++), and
Fortran (f90) with SALT-FM. To use them, configure TAU using:
$ ./configure -cc=clang -c++=clang++ -fortran=flang -openmp -ompt
$ make install

Then, with saltfm on your PATH (spack load saltfm):
$ export TAU_MAKEFILE=<taudir>/x86_64/lib/Makefile.tau-clang-ompt-openmp
$ cd c
$ ./run.sh

run.sh sets OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 and TAU_OMPT_SUPPORT_LEVEL=full. The
instrumented routines are called on thread 0, so pprof shows them on thread 0.
OMPT adds timers for the parallel regions and for each thread's share of the
loops, so pprof shows a profile for every thread.
